$DATUM N-(6-(5-Cyanopyridin-3-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide 8 A microwave
tube equipped with a magnetic stir bar was charged with
N-(6-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide
27 (50 mg, 0.157 mmol), 5-bromonicotinonitrile (50 mg, 0.273 mmol),
Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mg, 8.65 μmol), KOAc (1M, 0.40 mmol) and
N,N-dimethylacetate (2 mL). The tube was capped and the mixture was
subject to 15 min of microwave irradiation at 140 ºC. The reaction was
cooled, filtered and washed with water then DCM. The solid was slurried
in MeOH and concentrated and then slurried in ether and concentrated.
N-(6-(5-cyanopyridin-3-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide 8 (33 mg, 70%)
as a pale yellow solid. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 12.48 (br s, 1H),
9.26 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 9.01 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.71 (t, J = 2.1 Hz,
1H), 8.50-8.44 (m, 1H), 7.91 (dd, J = 2.1 Hz, 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.86 (d, J =
8.3 Hz, 1H), 2.23 (s, 3H); ESMS m/z 295.0 (M+ + 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling, microwave tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
