$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5,5'-Di-10-n-hexyl-10H-phenothiazin-[2,20]-bithiophene (2n). In a Schlenk
flask 5,50-diiodo-[2,2']-bithiophene (4f) (211 mg, 0.50 mmol),
10-hexyl-10H-phenothiazin-3-yl pinacolyl boronic ester (3) (409 mg, 1.00
mmol), and K2CO3 (276 mg, 2.00 mmol) dissolved in a mixture of DME (50
mL) and H2O (25 mL) are degassed in a stream of nitrogen for 10 min. Then
Pd(PPh3)4 (23 μmol, 26 mg) is added, and the reaction mixture is heated
to reflux temperature for 48 h. After cooling to room temperature, water
is added, and the aqueous phase is extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 50
mL). After drying of the organic layers with anhydrous magnesium sulfate,
the solvents are removed in vacuo. Upon concentration the product
precipitates and is collected by suction to give 2n (280 mg, 70%) as a
shiny orange solid. mp 146-148 °C. 1H NMR(300 MHz,CD2Cl2): δ 0.88 (m, 6
H), 1.26-1.34 (m, 8 H), 1.44 (mc, 4 H), 1.80 (mc, 4 H), 3.85 (t, J=7.2
Hz, 4 H), 6.87 (m, 4 H), 6.93 (m, 2 H), 7.1 (m, 6 H), 7.16 (m, 2 H), 7.35
(d, J= 1.9 Hz, 2 H), 7.38 (dd, J= 8.3 Hz, J= 2.2 Hz, 2 H). 13C NMR (75
MHz, CD2Cl2): δ 14.1 (CH3), 22.9 (CH2), 26.9 (CH2), 27.1 (CH2), 31.8
(CH2), 47.8 (CH2), 115.8 (CH), 115.9 (CH), 122.8 (CH), 123.3 (CH), 124.30
(CH), 124.31 (Cquat), 124.7 (CH), 124.8 (CH), 125.7 (Cquat), 127.6 (CH),
127.7 (CH), 128.7 (Cquat), 136.2 (Cquat), 142.4 (Cquat), 145.1 (Cquat),
145.2 (Cquat). FAB + MS m/z (%): 728 ([M - H] + , 6), 307 ([M - PT -C2HS]
+ , 100).UV-vis (CH2Cl2): λ max (ε) 250 nm (38300), 266 nm (37300), 338
nm (17800), 418 nm (4400). IR (KBr): ν~= 3061 cm-1, 1491, 1471, 1442,
1433, 1365, 1251, 1244, 798, 750. Anal. Calcd for C44H44N2S4 (729.1): C
72.48, H 6.08, N 3.84. Found: C 72.18, H 6.12, N 3.84.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
