$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-(2-Chloro-pyrimidin-4-yl)-furan-2-carbaldehyde (4c). To a degassed
(nitrogen) solution of 2,4-dichloropyrimidine 1a (3.8 g, 25.51 mmol) and
5-formyl-2-furan boronic acid (3 g, 21.44 mmol) in 1,2-dimethoxy ethane
[DME] (100 mL) were added aq. Na2CO3 (5.5 g in 10 mL of H2O, 51.0 mmol)
and Pd(dppf)Cl2 CH2Cl2 [1:1] (0.87 g, 1.07 mmol). The reaction mixture
was stirred to 80 °C for 4 h. It was cooled to rt and poured into water
and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 40 mL). The combined organic extracts were
washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced
pressure to obtain the crude residue. The crude material was purified by
column chromatography (EtOAc/Hexane 1:2) to afford 4c.
5-(2-Chloro-pyrimidin-4-yl)-furan-3-carbaldehyde (4n). The title compound
was synthesized from 1a and 4-formyl-2-furan boronic acid 3h (yield,
70%). LC-MS (ESI positive mode) m/z 209 ([M + H]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Suzuki coupling
