$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for Suzuki coupling reaction of intermediate 22. To a
vial containing corresponding boronic acid (0.5 mmol) was charged a stock
solution of
(R)-2'-bromo-7'-(neopentyloxy)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2-amine
(22) (0.050 g, 0.120 mmol), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0)
(0.014 g, 0.012 mmol), and dioxane (1.5 mL). A solution of potassium
carbonate (0.095 g, 0.688 mmol) and water (0.6 mL) was added. The
reaction was stirred overnight at 100°C. The mixture was diluted with
DMSO and filtered through a syringe filter, which was flushed with
additional DMSO. The material was purified via HPLC (10-90% MeCN:H2O w/
0.1% TFA of formic acid modifier) or chromatography on silica gel to
afford corresponding products as corresponding salts or free bases.
(S)-2'-(6-fluoropyridin-3-yl)-7'-(neopentyloxy)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2-amine
formate (27). Yield 69%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ = 8.48 (d, J=2.4
Hz, 1 H) 8.21 (td, J=8.2, 2.7 Hz, 1 H) 8.14 (s, 1 H) 7.66 (dd, J=8.4, 2.4
Hz, 1 H) 7.57 (d, J=2.3 Hz, 1 H) 7.29 (dd, J=8.8, 2.79 Hz, 1 H) 7.25 (d,
J=8.4 Hz, 1 H) 7.11 (d, J=8.9 Hz, 1 H) 6.94 (dd, J=8.9, 3.0 Hz, 1 H) 6.84
(d, J=2.9 Hz, 1 H) 4.22 (q, J=8.3 Hz, 2 H) 3.61 (q, J=8.6 Hz, 2 H) 1.01
(s, 9 H). MS m/z = 434.2 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Suzuki coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
