$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of P5. Monomer 5 (0.067 g, 0.14 mmol), monomer 9 (0.093 g, 0.14
mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (0.0025 g, 0.0027 mmol), HPtBu3BF4 (0.003 g, 0.01 mmol)
and N2-sparged aqueous potassium carbonate (2.0 M, 1.0 mL, 2.0 mmol) were
dissolved in 5 mL of THF in a Schlenk flask. The mixture was heated to 70
°C for 24 h and then 5 mL toluene was added. The reaction mixture was
stirred for another 48 h at 70 °C. The reaction mixture was then cooled
to room temperature, poured into 100 mL of water and extracted with 30 mL
of toluene. The organic layer was washed with 100 mL of brine and 100 mL
of water and then dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed in vacuo and
the residue was dissolved in 1 mL toluene, then reprecipitated in
methanol (200 mL); this procedure was repeated 3 times to give P5. Red
solid (0.071 g, 69 %). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.90 (s, thienyl-H),
2.89, 2.65, 1.74, 1.30, 0.90 (hexyl). 13C{1H} NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
145.1, 142.1, 142.0, 140.1, 133.6, 131.5, 129.3, 128.4 (aromatic C’s),
32.1, 31.8 30.1, 30.6, 29.3, 29.1, 28.1, 23.5, 23.3, 22.7, 14.3
(aliphatic C’s). Mn = 4.30 × 103, Mw = 6.97 × 104, PDI = 1.62 by GPC.
UV-vis (in THF): λmax = 429 nm, ε (per monomer repeat unit) = 1.82 × 104
L/(mol·cm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
