$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-(((3S,3aS)-7-(6-cyanopyridin-3-yl)-1-oxo-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide
(45). A mixture of 33a (50 mg, 0.147 mmol),
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)picolinonitrile1 (40.5 mg,
0.176 mmol), 2 N potassium fluoride (0.15mL, 0.30 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (17 mg, 0.015 mmol) in dioxane
(5 mL) was degassed and flushed with argon. The mixture was hearted to
reflux for 2 h. Dichloromethane/methanol (10:1, 50 mL) was added, and the
mixture was filtered, washed with water, saturated brine, dried over
sodium sulfate, and evaporated. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel with dichloromethane /methanol (50:1) to
give 45.
N-(((3S,3aS)-7-(2,4-dimethoxypyrimidin-5-yl)-1-oxo-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide
(50). Compound 50 (96 mg, 68.5%) was prepared from 33a (120 mg, 0.35
mmol) and
2,4-dimethoxy-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyrimidine
(124 mg, 1 mmol) in the same manner as described for 45. Mp: 210-212 °C
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.23 (s, 1 H), 8.05 (d, J = 9.03 Hz, 1 H),
7.15 (m, 2H), 6.00(t, J =7.32 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (d, J = 9.51 Hz, 1 H), 4.45
(m, 1 H), 4.05 (s, 6 H), 3.90-4.00 (m, 2 H), 3.70-3.78 (m, 2 H), 2.05 (s,
3 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 170.1, 167.4, 163.9, 157.5, 153.2,
143.8, 128.7, 122.8, 121.6, 118.1, 116.9, 114.6, 74.7, 65.8, 54.5, 54.0,
52.9, 40.5, 22.4. MS (EI) m/z: 400 (M+). HRMS (EI): Anal. Calcd for
C19H20N4O6: 400.1383, Found: 400.1376.
