$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure I.
(6S)-2-Nitro-6-({6-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-3-pyridazinyl}methoxy)-6,7-dihydro-5H-imidazo[2,1-b][1,3]oxazine
(104). A mixture of chloride 178 (0.100 g, 0.32 mmol) and
4-(trifluoromethyl)phenylboronic acid (0.073 g, 0.38 mmol) in toluene (5
mL), EtOH (3 mL), and aqueous K2CO3 (2M, 1 mL) was purged with N2 for 5
min. Pd(dppf)Cl2 (5mg, 6.83 μmol) was added, and the mixture was refluxed
under N2 for 0.5 h. The resulting solution was partitioned between EtOAc
and water, and the organic layer was dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under
reduced pressure.Columnchromatography of the residue on silica gel,
eluting with 1:1 hexanes:EtOAc and 0-5% MeOH/EtOAc,
(6S)-6-{[6-(6-Methoxy-3-pyridinyl)-3-pyridazinyl]methoxy}-2-nitro-6,7-dihydro-5H-imidazo[
2,1-b][1,3]oxazine (111). Reaction of chloride 178 and
6-methoxy-3-pyridinylboronic acid under the Suzuki coupling conditions
described in Procedure I gave 111 (69%) as a white solid: mp 186-190 °C;
1H NMR [(CD3)2SO] δ 8.93 (dd, J = 2.4, 0.6 Hz, 1 H), 8.45 (dd, J = 8.7,
2.5 Hz, 1 H), 8.25 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 1 H), 8.03 (s, 1 H), 7.73 (d, J = 8.9
Hz, 1 H), 7.00 (dd, J = 8.7, 0.6 Hz, 1 H), 5.01 (d, J = 13.2 Hz, 1 H),
4.98 (d, J = 13.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.73 (dt, J = 12.1, 2.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.51 (br d,
J = 11.9 Hz, 1 H), 4.42-4.32 (m, 2 H), 4.27 (dd, J = 13.5, 3.2 Hz, 1 H),
3.94 (s, 3 H). Anal. (C17H16N6O5) C, H. N: calcd, 21.87; found, 21.46.
HPLC purity: 98.5%.
