$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-(((3S,3aS)-7-(4-acetylphenyl)-1-oxo-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide
(40). A mixture of 34 (120 mg, 0.309 mmol), 2 N cesium carbonate (0.31
mL, 0.62 mmol), 1-(4-bromophenyl)ethanone (73.8 mg, 0.37 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (35.7mg, 0.03 mmol) in dioxane
(6 mL) was degassed and flushed with argon. The mixture was hearted at 80
°C for 2 h. Dichloromethane (30 mL) was added, and the mixture was
filtered through Celite, washed with water, saturated brine, dried over
sodium sulfate, and evaporated. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel with dichloromethane /methanol (50:1) to
give 40.
N-(((3S,3aS)-7-(2-aminopyrimidin-5-yl)-1-oxo-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide
(51). Compound 51 (96 mg, 68.5%) was prepared from 34 (120 mg, 0.309
mmol) and 5-bromopyrimidin-2-amine (64.5 mg, 0.37 mmol) in the same
manner as described for 40. Mp: 243-245 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ
8.56 (s, 1H), 8.31 (t, 1 H), 7.92 (d, J = 9.16 Hz, 1 H), 7.28 (m, 2 H),
4.55 (d, J = 7.33 Hz, 1 H), 4.50 (d, J = 6.72 Hz, 1 H), 3.95-4.08 (m, 2
H), 3.50-3.58 (m, 2 H),1.87 (s, 3 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 170.1,
162.8, 155.7 (2 C, overlap), 153.2, 144.6, 131.3, 122.4, 122.3, 121.2,
121.1, 118.8, 118.1, 113.2, 74.7, 65.8, 53.0, 40.5, 40.1, 39.9, 39.7,
39.6, 39.5, 39.3, 39.1, 38.9, 22.4. MS (EI) m/z: 355 (M+). HRMS (EI):
Anal. Calcd for C17H17N5O4: 355.1281, Found: 355.1287.
