$DATUM 8-Chloro-7-(7-chloro-1H-indol-5-yl)-3-(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl)-imidazo[1,2-a]pyridine
(27o). To a mixture of 6c (0.21 g, 0.58 mmol) and 13k (0.18 g, 0.64 mmol)
in a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (1.5 mL) and 1,4-dioxane (3.5
mL) was added Pd(PPh3)4 (0.034 g, 0.029 mmol). The mixture was heated at
150 °C for 10 min under microwave irradiation. The mixture was cooled to
room temperature and filtered through a Celite pad. The filtrate was
diluted with water (10 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 10 mL). The
organic layer was washed with brine (10 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
and the volatiles were evaporated in vacuo. The residue thus obatained
was purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc in CH2Cl2,
0/100 to 30/70) to give 27o. Pale white solid, yield (0.09 g, 69%). Mp
182.8 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.78 (q, J= 9.9 Hz, 2H), 6.68 (dd, J=
3.1, 2.2 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.35 (broad t, J= 2.8 Hz, 1H),
7.39 (d, J= 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.72 (broad d, J= 0.7 Hz, 1H), 7.74 (s, 1H),
8.00 (d, J= 6.9 Hz, 1H), 8.57 (broad s, 1H). LC-MS: m/z 384 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Imidazo[1,2-a]pyridines: Orally Active Positive Allosteric Modulators of
the Metabotropic Glutamate 2 Receptor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Trabanco, Andres A.; Tresadern, Gary; Macdonald, Gregor J.; Vega, Juan
