$DATUM 8-(3-Chloro-5-(prop-1-en-2-yl)pyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]-decan-1-one
(58). 8-(3-Bromo-5-chloropyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro- [4.5]decan-1-one
(57) (200 mg, 0.580 mmol), isopropenylboronic acid (120 μL, 0.638 mmol),
and Pd(dppf)Cl2·CH2Cl2 (24 mg, 0.029 mmol) were loaded in a microwave
vial under argon, and then acetonitrile (10.4 mL) and 0.5 M aqueous
sodium carbonate solution (1.60 mL, 0.812 mmol) were added. The reaction
mixture was heated at 120 °C for 60 min under microwave irradiation,
concentrated, and purified via Biotage column chromatography (DCM/EtOH
99:1 to 95:5). 8-(3-chloro-5-(prop-1-en-2-yl)pyridin-4-yl)-2,8-
diazaspiro[4.5]decan-1-one (58) as a colorless oil (122 mg, 69% yield).
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.50−1.56 (m, 2H), 2.07−2.14 (m, 5H), 2.16 (t,
J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 3.15−3.20 (m, 2H), 3.36−3.42 (m, 4H), 4.97−4.98 (m, 1H),
5.26−5.28 (m, 1H), 5.81 (s, 1H), 8.15 (s, 1H), 8.39 (s, 1H); LC−MS
(method C, ESI, m/z) t R = 1.78 min, 306/ 308 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, thermal, microwave vial used,
Suzuki coupling
