$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Biaryls 1-10 and 14-32. Heteroaryl halide (0.30 mmol),
(4-methoxyphenyl)boronic acid (0.39 mmol), potassium carbonate (0.90
mmol), and Pd0-AmP-MCF (3.99 mg, 0.003 mmol) were suspended in a 1:1
mixture of ethanol (95% aq)/water (2 mL) in a microwave vial. The sealed
vial was heated at 90 °C (fixed hold time, normal absorption) for an
appropriate time in a microwave reactor. The mixture was diluted with
dichloromethane and washed with water. The phases were separated. The
organic phase was run through a phase separator and purified by flash
chromatography using a gradient of ethyl acetate/heptane to give the
desired product after evaporation of solvent. Purification by flash
chromatography using a gradient of ethyl acetate/heptane, 0 → 40% ethyl
acetate afforded the Product. 5-(6-Methoxypyridin-3-yl)pyrimidine (32).
Purification by flash chromatography using a gradient of ethyl
acetate/heptane, 40 → 80% ethyl acetate afforded 38 mg (68%) of 32 as a
light beige solid; Time: 1 h. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.22 (s, 1H),
8.92 (s, 2H), 8.41 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 7.80 (dd, J = 8.6, 2.6 Hz, 1H),
6.91 (dd, J = 8.6, 0.5 Hz, 1H), 4.01 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ
164.7, 157.5, 154.4, 145.2, 137.0, 131.5, 123.3, 111.7, 53.8; HRMS (ESI+)
m/z calculated for [C10H9N3O + H+]: 188.0824, found 188.0811.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, catalysts reusable, sealed tube used, Suzuki
coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
