$DATUM (e)
Diethyl-2,2’:5’,2”:5”,2”’:5’”,2””:5””,2””’-sexithiophene-3”,4’”-dicarboxylate
(eq. (5)) Aqueous solution (0.50 mL) of potassium carbonate (0.12 g, 0.85
mmol) and a THF solution (5.0 mL) of
5-(4,4,5,5-tertramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-2,2'-bithiophene (0.18
g, 0.62 mmol) were added to a THF solution (3.0 mL) of
diethyl-5,5’-dibromo-2,2’-bithiophene-4,4’-carboxylate (0.12 g, 0.26
mmol) and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0.030 g, 0.026 mmol)
under argon. The reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h at 75°C. After the
reaction, the precipitate was collected and washed with portions of
water, THF and toluene to obtain the product as an orange solid in a 68%
yield (0.11 g). mp. 229−230°C. 1H NMR (500 MHz,in CDCl3, 30°C ) δ 7.55
(s, 1H, C4”,3”’H), 7.46 (d, 1H, C4”,3”’H, J = 3.9 Hz), 7.25 (1H, C
5,5””’H, overlapped with CDCl3), 7.26 (1H, C3,3””’H, overlapped with
CDCl3), 7.15 (d, 1H, C3’,4””H, J = 3.9 Hz), 7.04 (dd, 1H, C4,4””’H, J =
5.1 Hz, 3.7 Hz), 4.37 (q, 2H, −CH2−), 1.38 (t, 3H, −CH3). 13C NMR (125
MHz, in CDCl3, 30°C ) δ 162.3, 141.7, 139.7, 136.3, 132.8, 131.7, 129.9,
127.5, 126.7, 124.7, 123.8, 123.4, 60.6, 13.8.MALDI-TOF MS m/z = 637.4
([M+H]+, calc. 639.0). Anal. Calcd for C30H22O4S6: C, 56.40; H, 3.47.
Found: C, 56.54; H, 3.43.
