$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2. To a suspension of 2-fluoropyridin-4-ylboronic acid (2.26 g, 16.0
mmol) and 6-chloro-N-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)pyrimidin-4-amine (2.85 g,
13.3 mmol) in 100 mL 4:1 dioxane/water was added sodium carbonate (4.24
g, 40.0 mmol) and the suspension was purged with argon. To this was added
PdCl2(dppf)*dcm (0.545 g, 0.667 mmol) and the mixture heated at 80 °C
under nitrogen. After stirring for 6 hours, the reaction mixture was
cooled, diluted with water and extracted with EtOAc two times. The
organics were washed with water, brine, dried and evaporated. The crude
product was purified by chromatography on silica gel, eluted with 50-70%
EtOAc/hexanes,
6-(2-fluoropyridin-4-yl)-N-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)pyrimidin-4-amine
(2.50 g, 68 % yield) as tan solids. m/z (APCI-pos) M+1 = 275.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Highly Potent, Selective, and Efficacious Small Molecule
Inhibitors of ERK1/2
