$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Polymer PHHA-BT. Compound 6 (0.25 g, 0.259 mmol),
benzo[c]-1,2,3-thiadiazol-4,7-diyl-4,7-diboronic acid dipinacol ester
(0.102 g, 0.259 mmol), 20 mL of K2CO3 solution (2 M in H2O) were added
into a three neck flask containing 50 mL of toluene. The flask was
connected to a reflux condenser and filled with nitrogen. After bubbling
the toluene solution for 30 mins, 20 mg of Pd(PPh3)4 was added. The
degassed reaction mixture was stirred under nitrogen at 95 °C for two
days. Workup of the reaction mixture and isolation of the polymer
occurred by extraction with chloroform, washing of the combined organic
extracts with 1 M HCl, sat. aqueous NaHCO3 solution, water and drying
over MgSO4. Then this organic extract was filtered through a short
florisil column. After partial evaporation of the solvent, the
concentrated solution was precipitated into methanol and the solid was
collected by filtration and extracted in a Soxhlet setup with methanol
for 24 hours, and then with hexane for another 24 hours. The remainders
were redissolved in chloroform and precipitated into methanol. After
filtration and drying in vacuo at 50 °C overnight, the polymer was
obtained, yield 0.17 g, 68%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 8.22-7.23 (m,
6H), 6.33 (bs, 2H), 2.80-0.70 (m, 69H), GPC: Mn = 2.9 kg/mol, Mw = 6.8
kg/mol, PDI=2.30.
